Call source callbacks as what they really are: a callback given as another type than the one it is
called as (a gboolean function as a GChildWatchFunc: GSubprocess; a void one as a GSourceFunc)
traps on WebAssembly, which checks the type of every call through a pointer. Uses the add-on's
libffi (ffi_wasm_call) when the program has it.

